(Menger; vertex version for digraphs). \emph{Let \texttt{x} and \texttt{y} be two
vertices of a digraph \texttt{D} such that \texttt{x} is not joined to \texttt{y}. Then
the maximum number of internally-disjoint directed \texttt{(x, y)}-paths in \texttt{D}
is equal to the minimum number of vertices whose deletion destroys all directed
\texttt{(x, y)}-paths.}
